WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.930
and Mrs. North starring Barbara Britton and Richard Denning.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:32.500
Thank you.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:08.270
Brina, Jessie, Vivian, oh...

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:30.000
Next door, Francois. What do you want?

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.450
Here is the list for the lonely grocery and the dismal vegetables.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:39.540
I also like to have a million dollars, a year's vacation, and you.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.780
You watch your language.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.460
- Maggie, Maggie!

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:07.450
- Oh, John, you're gonna come put me down.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.530
- Hey, is that any way for a bride to act?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.330
- I'm not your bride.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.450
- Well, you will be in a few hours, it's all set.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.940
- Well then, I'm set it.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.660
I'm sorry, John, but I can't.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.570
- Can't?

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:26.470
- Well, I didn't hear from you for so many years, I thought.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.920
- Five years, I know.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.890
- Those years were spent in the pen, Maggie.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.780
- Oh.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.690
- It taught me a lot.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.590
It made me realize you were the most important thing

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.860
in my life.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.050
I used to dream at night about this day,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.770
the day I claimed you as my wife.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.030
- Oh, no, John, please.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.980
- Oh, don't worry.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.550
I'm not in the racket anymore.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.290
The old big John you knew is gone.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.910
- I'm glad, for your sake.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:59.380
But I can't marry you, John, it's impossible.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.000
Try and understand.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:09.280
- Look. Let's talk this over. - Hello, Mrs. North. Welcome back.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.280
- Thank you, beginner. - We've been looking forward to this for a whole year.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:17.100
Oh, listen, Mr. Thornton. John, meet Mr. and Mrs. North, my favorite guest.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.100
- How do you do, Mr. Thornton? - Say, is Francois still your chef?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:24.600
- Of course. - Oh, Mr. and Mrs. North, I've gotten as you can outside.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.980
- Madame North. - Monsieur! - Francois!

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.540
- It is such a pleasure to see you.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.620
Hello, Greek kings.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.160
Wait, wait, wait, don't tell me.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.540
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, number 5, honeymoon, right.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.460
- I can't see you in your rooms, will you excuse me?

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.560
- Of course.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:52.950
- Quel amour, what love.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.120
This reminds me of the springtime in Paris.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.960
- Oh, we remember Paris all right.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.000
We also remember your cooking.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.980
For a year I've been dreaming of your sauces and gravies and lobsters and champagne.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.680
Ah, a man who dreams like that, a priest made the art of living.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.180
And the snails in garlic, and the kidneys in port.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.180
And you in the hospital.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.480
What death could be more blissful than from eating?

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.290
Well, I guess it depends on who's cooking.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.790
Oh, I adore you, darling, but even you don't enjoy your cooking.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.490
I know, darn it, you're right.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.290
I guess I need some lessons, Francois.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.000
Oh, I think...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.940
I hear something in the kitchen is bumbling.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:33.890
Hey, cow eyes.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.130
Scrum in the kitchen.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.710
You wanted to talk.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.360
Now, what is it, John?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.820
Is it Frank?

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:45.750
Yes.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.190
I'll soon change that.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.280
When he hears what I've got to tell him about you,

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.860
he'll drop you like a hot potato.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:54.690
It won't work.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.740
I've already told him everything.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.230
We have no secrets from each other.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.000
That's real touching.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.940
- Did you tell him about the box?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:03.790
- The box?

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:05.240
- The safe deposit box.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.870
The one that's in both our names.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.850
The one you're paying rent for.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.400
You've got the key to it.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.330
- What about it?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.420
- Don't horse around, Maggie.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.470
There's almost $50,000 in that box.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.210
Cold cash.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.530
- I don't believe it.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.120
- It's the truth.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.640
- Racket money.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.010
And you hid it in my name.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.040
I could have wound up in jail myself.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.000
- That money was for us.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.030
That's where I've been, on the spot every day for five years.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.030
And you, you tried to tell me you love me.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.030
All right, all right. Give me the key. I'll get you off the hook.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:43.590
The key? Banks got that too.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:46.750
What? You're joking.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.750
No, I gave him everything.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.890
My bank books, the hotel papers, the key.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.030
I still have the rent receipts on the box, but...

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.480
Why, you must have been out of your mind.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:16.570
- He's got everything. - Everything.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.050
Ah, the Seraph Logan. Hello, Frank.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:30.000
- How's the business of crime? - I guess it's here to stay.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.290
- How's the cooking business? - I cook, people eat.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.630
People stop eating, I stop cooking.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.240
Then we're all out of business.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:44.460
Why, Mademoiselle Margaret, she is out, but she's gonna be back shortly.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.860
I didn't come to see her today.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.860
- No? Who else? - Maybe you.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:54.400
Me? Gastronomically or officially?

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.600
It's official, Francois.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:00.000
Sometimes it ain't no fun being sheriff. No fun at all.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.480
Sometimes it faces a man with a mighty unpleasant duty.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.710
Yeah, like a husband who has to go home to the wife, he don't love it.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.400
The shorty, the French police?

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.700
Yeah, sure is.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.460
Yeah, well, whatever it is, they want you.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.780
Me?

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:22.870
But I am so unimportant and just a little honey in the chicken fricassee.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:25.110
It is extradition papers.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.760
Bigamy.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.270
I'm Francois. He's cooked.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.060
Beg your pardon.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.280
We best go now.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.930
No, no. No, no. Not till I'm finished my coccovain.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.310
You haven't any choice.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.750
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:51.450
But you don't stop an artist in the middle of a brushstroke.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:56.130
When my coccovain is finished, his positivity is a masterpiece.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.000
So you wait. You wait. Come on.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:06.050
Come on, now you wait, and while you wait, you eat.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.180
These only take a couple, two, three hours.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.020
Reckon it wouldn't hurt to let you finish it at that.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:25.740
Always knew you were romantic, cuz, but I sure never figured you for four wives.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.000
You never spend it for springtime in Paris.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:35.870
Ah, poor Francois, I never can say no to a lady.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.220
It's worth three more which I divorced.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.140
What expenses!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.660
Uh-huh.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.090
Well, which one's gonna get you?

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.030
They all want you back.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.880
You can put the names in the hut.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.390
I don't mind to go to jail.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:53.810
But to go back to those women, never!

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.890
Never I go back to those women!

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:27.090
- You don't have any choice.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:30.000
- Trouble, they start in the cradle and end

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.580
I guess you are right. Where is Agnes?

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.470
She is sitting at the table for dinner.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:43.240
Oh, no, no. I do this for you.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.240
Thank you, François.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.240
Yes, you are tired and you want to get clean up for dinner.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:58.680
Oh, have you seen Sheriff Logan?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.760
No, I don't see the Serif today.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.960
Oh, well, he'll get here in time for dinner.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:13.220
He always does.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.220
And does what he has to do.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:00.000
For the moonlight ride, I fall overboard for the guests.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.200
With a woman.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.200
No, that's not the attitude, Francois.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.200
Oh, Mrs. North, I don't always want to be you.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.200
That's all I gathered.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.200
Here, let me help you.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.200
Oh, no, no, no, not with my cocoa vac.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.200
Now, tomorrow, you take first lesson, but tonight, you just watch.

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.060
All right, tonight, I watch.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.110
I don't...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.820
You really should butcher those chickens outside.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:41.970
- Give me the towel, I clean them up. - Well, at least I can help you put these away.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:53.440
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, I need these on the outside.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:12:00.000
Maybe, maybe you help me with the cook-a-vex, I can't help you, I can't help you, I can't help you.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:18.740
I may not be a king, but I've just eaten like one.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:24.830
Brandy would be just right to celebrate your fifth honeymoon.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:27.900
I've been saving a special bottle for you in the pantry.

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.160
Oh, wonderful.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:43.270
- She's fainted, get some water.

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.850
- Water.

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:48.550
- Jerry, is he?

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.910
- Yes, better call the sheriff.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:57.150
- He's no use, that is the sheriff.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.020
We'll take her up to her room so she can rest.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.000
Call the sheriff's deputy.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:13.040
He doesn't seem strange to you, Ms. McGinnis fainting that way.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.060
She doesn't seem the type.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.060
Now, Pam, don't stop.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.040
Well, I was just wondering.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:28.740
You know, Pam, I was just...

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.800
- Jerry, look, the killer must have dropped it.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.600
The chain's broken.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.470
- Looks like a wedding ring.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.820
- Initials?

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.270
- F.L.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:51.150
- L. Jerry, what's Francois' last name?

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:52.770
- F.L.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:53.610
