The Sheriff's wallet.

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:20.350
You sure?

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:23.350
Sure, I'm sure. He's trying to sneak it back in with the Sheriff's thing.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.360
Oh, no, no. I find it in your pocket.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:28.360
Oh, you found it in your pocket, huh? You expect me to believe that story?

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.000
Oh, you're wrong, Monsieur. I'm not sure.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.170
You're under arrest for murder.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:04.320
The wedding ring, and it's just like the other one.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.030
I knew it.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:28.480
Robert McGinnis and Frank Logan, and he barked.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.640
- What are you doing here?

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:04.510
- Visiting Maggie.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.450
Where are you taking those papers?

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.740
- They're mine.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.030
Some letters from my business files.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:10.850
- That isn't true.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.530
One of them's a marriage license

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:15.270
and the others are receipts for a safety,

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.890
safety deposit box.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:21.490
Did the sheriff have the key to that?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.170
- I don't quite know what you're talking about.

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:27.380
- There was a key missing from the sheriff's key ring

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.730
and he and Maggie were secretly married.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.850
Why, Mrs. North, you've been reading too many detective stories.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.590
Have I? Excuse me, I want to find my husband.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:42.450
Oh, Agnes, have you seen Mr. North?

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.520
I think Mr. North took a stroll down to the lake.

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:46.520
He said he was going there.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.080
Thank you.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:48.550
Don't bother to scream Mrs. Knopf.

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:50.980
Your husband is way down by the lake.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.890
What are you going to do?

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:56.130
You know too much.

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.990
You killed Frank Logan.

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:00.000
I said you know.

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:02.600
I don't know too much.

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.480
- Hey, Jerry, is he hurt badly?

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:15.460
- No, Francois keeps that shotgun for chicken thieves.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.070
It was only loaded with rock salt.

00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:19.750
He'll have a nice mess of blisters, though,

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:25.770
but they'll heal up in time for him to sit in an electric chair.

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:26.970
- Midnight snack.

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:30.000
Francois, this is more like a seven-day feast.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.140
Permit me. I'm Pierre Toussaint of the French Sûreté.

00:23:33.690 --> 00:23:35.950
Sheriff Rogan was to deliver Francois.

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:38.490
Wait, you mean Francois is under arrest?

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:41.830
Oui. His wives are pressing charges to bigamy.

00:23:42.250 --> 00:23:44.590
I have here the original extradition papers.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.000
Only on one condition I make the surrender.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:50.350
I return to the jail, but not to those wives.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:53.760
The crime is not called for such terrifical punishment.

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:55.120
Calm yourself.

00:23:55.120 --> 00:24:00.000
already parished jails, is waiting for your rival to replace their abominable cook.

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:05.590
A wretch of a man whose cooking untitles him only to the guillotine.

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:09.910
You see, Miss Amy, I have nothing else to do but say goodbye.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:11.780
Oh, the rabbit, the rabbit.

00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:15.380
Let him simmer and turn him off in half hour.

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:19.320
Yes, I think I take a hamburger for the trip.

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:29.960
- Jerry, can't you do something? - Like what, madame Noor?

00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:33.480
Au revoir. Monsieur Nuret.

00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:36.220
So long, sport. Goodbye, friend.

00:24:37.130 --> 00:24:38.140
I surrender.

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:42.970
Au revoir, monsieur.

00:24:43.070 --> 00:24:46.410
Avec plaisir. Adieu.

00:25:06.810 --> 00:25:09.810
Mr. and Mrs. North is directed by Ralph Francis Murphy.

00:25:10.910 --> 00:25:12.830
A John W. Lovedon production.

00:25:14.090 --> 00:25:16.350
Produced by Federal Telefilms.

00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:19.030
Starring Barbara Britton and Richard Denning.

00:25:19.170 --> 00:25:20.630
Featuring Francis DeSales.

00:25:34.320 --> 00:25:36.340
This has been a film presentation.
